132
00:06:05,448 --> 00:06:07,367
-I love it. It's a good keepsake.
-Right?

133
00:06:07,951 --> 00:06:08,952
I'm thinking this one.

134
00:06:10,245 --> 00:06:12,330
It has the train on it.

135
00:06:12,414 --> 00:06:13,874
[Machu] Oh, you're right.

136
00:06:15,333 --> 00:06:16,334
[Shime] How cute.

137
00:06:18,086 --> 00:06:19,087
Mmm.

138
00:06:21,715 --> 00:06:23,049
[Shime, in English] 20.74.

139
00:06:23,133 --> 00:06:24,509
[in Japanese] Then… this one.

140
00:06:24,593 --> 00:06:26,261
-[in English] Thank you.
-[Machu, in Japanese] It's really cute.

141
00:06:26,344 --> 00:06:27,721
I'm happy with this purchase.

142
00:06:30,015 --> 00:06:31,850
-[Genta] Isn't this crazy, or what?
-This is nuts.

143
00:06:32,601 --> 00:06:34,644
-[Genta] It's outta this world.
-This is wild.

144
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:38,356
-[Genta] Are you excited?
-Oh, very.

145
00:06:38,857 --> 00:06:40,609
-[Genta] Not exaggerating?
-It's too close!

146
00:06:40,692 --> 00:06:42,360
[in English]
You guys wanna come in the engine?

147
00:06:42,444 --> 00:06:43,445
Oh, yeah.

148
00:06:43,528 --> 00:06:46,031
-Come on.
-Let's go. Come on!

149
00:06:46,114 --> 00:06:47,657
-Let's go!
-[in Japanese] Whoa, no way.

150
00:06:47,741 --> 00:06:49,743
-It's massive.
-Whoa, we get to hop onboard!

151
00:06:50,368 --> 00:06:51,369
Wowee.

152
00:06:51,453 --> 00:06:52,537
[conductor, in English]
Come up the ladder.

153
00:06:52,621 --> 00:06:53,622
Okay.

154
00:06:53,705 --> 00:06:54,706
[in Japanese] This is sick.

155
00:06:55,373 --> 00:06:56,541
[in English] Ooh!

156
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:58,168
Whoa!

157
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:00,754
-[conductor] Everything's burning hot.
-[Machu, in Japanese] Whoa, no way.

158
00:07:00,837 --> 00:07:01,921
[in English] Wow.

159
00:07:02,005 --> 00:07:04,591
-[Shime, in Japanese] I can't believe it.
-[in English] Awesome.

160
00:07:06,343 --> 00:07:08,303
[Genta, Machu, Shime, in Japanese] Whoa!

161
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:10,513
[Machu] This is how the engine
is powered up.

162
00:07:10,597 --> 00:07:12,223
[Genta] Does it go, "choo-choo?"
Choo-choo.

163
00:07:12,307 --> 00:07:15,226
-[Shime, in English] I wanna try… Yeah.
-[conductor] Blow the whistle?

164
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:17,562
We'll do that later.
If I blow that now, it means something.

165
00:07:17,646 --> 00:07:19,022
-[Machu] Okay, later.
-[Shime] Ah, okay.

166
00:07:19,105 --> 00:07:21,608
-[conductor] It would confuse everybody.
-Okay.

167
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:23,276
-[in Japanese] Whoa, no way.
-It's sick.

168
00:07:24,319 --> 00:07:25,487
[Shime] I'm blown away.

169
00:07:25,570 --> 00:07:26,946
[Genta] What a special experience.

170
00:07:28,406 --> 00:07:30,533
[conductor, in English] Yes.
These are all the engineer's controls.

171
00:07:30,617 --> 00:07:32,535
-Got all of our brakes. Brake systems.
-[Shime] Uh-huh.

172
00:07:32,619 --> 00:07:33,620
-Brake. Okay.
-[Genta] Oh.

173
00:07:33,703 --> 00:07:35,622
-This is our gas pedal and throttle.
-[Machu] Okay.

174
00:07:35,705 --> 00:07:38,333
And then this is how we change direction.
To go forward, go backward.

175
00:07:38,416 --> 00:07:40,877
[Machu, in Japanese] This is how
the train engineer controls the train.

176
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:42,003
[Shime] Who knew. How amazing.

177
00:07:42,087 --> 00:07:43,380
[in English] This is Lane.
He's our fireman.

178
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,464
[Genta] Hi.

179
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:47,967
He sits here and controls the fuel,
and makes the fire bigger and smaller,

180
00:07:48,051 --> 00:07:49,761
-and adjust the steam pressure.
-[Shime] Okay.

181
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:50,887
Puts water in the boiler.

182
00:07:50,970 --> 00:07:52,305
[Machu] What is this?

183
00:07:52,389 --> 00:07:54,015
[conductor] Oh, all of these? Yeah.

184
00:07:54,099 --> 00:07:57,769
So, these are all valves that control
different aspects of the engine.

185
00:07:57,852 --> 00:07:59,646
-[Machu] Uh-huh.
-Um, they're just main shut-offs.

186
00:07:59,729 --> 00:08:02,941
So, we can shut steam off to an appliance
if something were to, you know,

187
00:08:03,024 --> 00:08:04,317
break open or something.

188
00:08:04,401 --> 00:08:07,153
Uh, if we need to isolate something,
we can do that.

189
00:08:07,237 --> 00:08:09,155
-[Machu] Uh-huh.
-Um, this is just a vent.

190
00:08:09,239 --> 00:08:11,157
It opens up the roof
so it doesn't get so hot.

191
00:08:11,241 --> 00:08:12,367
[Machu] Ah, I see, I see.

192
00:08:12,450 --> 00:08:14,411
[conductor] It's still hot,
but that kind of helps.

193
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:15,704
-[Genta] Uh-huh.
-[conductor] Um…

194
00:08:15,787 --> 00:08:18,415
and then this is steam pressure
in the boiler.

195
00:08:19,082 --> 00:08:21,501
-[Genta] A boiler.
-[Machu] Boiler. Ah, I see.

196
00:08:21,584 --> 00:08:22,585
[Genta] Cool.

197
00:08:23,253 --> 00:08:24,379
[in Japanese]
Man, this is really exciting.

198
00:08:24,462 --> 00:08:25,463
-[Genta] Whoa, this is cool.
-Right?

199
00:08:25,547 --> 00:08:27,215
-Normally, you can't access this area.
-[Genta] Right?

200
00:08:27,298 --> 00:08:29,718
-I'm over the moon.
-We're super excited!

201
00:08:30,218 --> 00:08:32,387
-[Genta] Shime-chan's stoked.
-[in English] Let's go!

202
00:08:32,470 --> 00:08:33,555
[Genta, in Japanese] Here we go.

203
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:34,848
-[in English] Thank you.
-[conductor] Yeah.

204
00:08:34,931 --> 00:08:35,932
Thank you so much.

205
00:08:36,516 --> 00:08:38,184
-Appreciate it.
-Yeah, no problem.

206
00:08:38,268 --> 00:08:39,352
[Machu] Thank you.

207
00:08:39,436 --> 00:08:40,520
[Genta] Whoo.

208
00:08:41,813 --> 00:08:43,940
-There you go.
-Thank you so much.

209
00:08:44,023 --> 00:08:46,526
-Turn around.
-Turn around. Thank you.

210
00:08:48,820 --> 00:08:50,113
-Thank you. Good job.
-Thank you.

211
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:51,364
-Thank you.
-Thank you so much.

212
00:08:51,448 --> 00:08:53,033
-Sure, have fun.
-Thank you so much.

213
00:08:53,575 --> 00:08:54,951
[in Japanese] How cool.
It's not every day you get to…

214
00:08:55,035 --> 00:08:56,119
What a special experience.

215
00:08:56,202 --> 00:08:57,662
-…see the steam engine up close.
-Right?

216
00:08:57,746 --> 00:08:58,955
-That was crazy.
-Seriously.

217
00:09:09,257 --> 00:09:10,341
[♪ upbeat music playing]

218
00:09:10,425 --> 00:09:12,093
-Well, shall we board the train?
-[Shime] Is it time?

219
00:09:12,177 --> 00:09:13,178
[Machu] Let's go.

220
00:09:13,261 --> 00:09:14,721
-[in English] Hello.
-Hello.

221
00:09:14,804 --> 00:09:15,889
[Machu, in Japanese] Yes, let's.

222
00:09:17,432 --> 00:09:18,933
-[in English] Oh, yeah.
-[in Japanese] Hup-ho.

223
00:09:19,017 --> 00:09:20,018
[Shime] Whoa, whoa, whoa.

224
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:21,603
[Machu, in English] Hello.

225
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:22,854
[Genta] Oh, yeah.

226
00:09:22,937 --> 00:09:24,522
[in Japanese] Wowza. [in English] Hi.

227
00:09:24,606 --> 00:09:25,774
-[passengers] Hi.
-[Shime] Hello.

228
00:09:25,857 --> 00:09:27,400
[Genta] Hello. Hello.

229
00:09:28,151 --> 00:09:29,652
[Machu, in Japanese]
Whoa, no freaking way.

230
00:09:29,736 --> 00:09:30,737
[Shime] Right?

231
00:09:32,655 --> 00:09:34,699
