471
00:21:02,470 --> 00:21:03,554
-[Machu] Uh-huh.
-[Shime] Twice a week?

472
00:21:03,637 --> 00:21:05,514
Just twice a week. Tuesdays and Saturdays.

473
00:21:05,598 --> 00:21:06,640
[Genta] Uh-huh.

474
00:21:06,724 --> 00:21:10,978
But then tourism picked up
in this area in the mid-1950s

475
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:13,355
and the train started running
every day then.

476
00:21:13,439 --> 00:21:14,440
[Genta] Wow.

477
00:21:14,523 --> 00:21:19,570
And this railroad has survived
two floods, um, economic disaster,

478
00:21:20,070 --> 00:21:23,741
um, the collapse of the mining industry,
the Great Depression

479
00:21:23,824 --> 00:21:25,367
and it still soldiered on

480
00:21:25,451 --> 00:21:26,744
-through these mountains.
-[Genta] Wow.

481
00:21:26,827 --> 00:21:29,163
-[in Japanese] How inspiring.
-[in English] So cool.

482
00:21:29,246 --> 00:21:30,956
[conductor]
I mean, like, it is pretty cool.

483
00:21:31,040 --> 00:21:32,750
-It's definitely very different.
-Yeah.

484
00:21:32,833 --> 00:21:35,753
You won't find another railroad
like this anywhere in the world.

485
00:21:35,836 --> 00:21:37,922
-Mmm.
-Mm-hmm, mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

486
00:21:38,005 --> 00:21:39,006
Wow.

487
00:21:39,089 --> 00:21:42,384
A couple places rival it,
but this place is pretty spectacular.

488
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:43,636
-[Shime] Wow.
-[Machu] Uh-huh.

489
00:21:43,719 --> 00:21:47,097
[Machu, in Japanese]
Do you get a lot of snow in this region?

490
00:21:47,181 --> 00:21:49,642
[in English] Uh, yes.
We do get a lot of snow, and we, uh…

491
00:21:49,725 --> 00:21:51,852
we do run the train in the winter as well.

492
00:21:51,936 --> 00:21:54,522
And we'll put a snowplow
on the front of the engine

493
00:21:54,605 --> 00:21:57,525
to clear the snow off of the tracks
in the wintertime.

494
00:21:57,608 --> 00:21:59,777
-Really fun to see that happening.
-Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

495
00:21:59,860 --> 00:22:00,861
I see.

496
00:22:00,945 --> 00:22:02,446
[in Japanese]
It can't be easy. Dealing with the snow.

497
00:22:02,530 --> 00:22:04,782
Have you seen a Christmas movie
with a train in it?

498
00:22:04,865 --> 00:22:06,992
-There's always a snowplow at the front.
-Right.

499
00:22:07,076 --> 00:22:08,953
-Right, right, right.
-It has the plow attached.

500
00:22:09,036 --> 00:22:10,037
That's so true. Yeah.

501
00:22:10,120 --> 00:22:12,039
-That thing.
-I'd reckon, yeah.

502
00:22:12,122 --> 00:22:13,707
It's incredible.

503
00:22:13,791 --> 00:22:15,793
I'll bet the experience is different
with snow.

504
00:22:15,876 --> 00:22:18,045
-[Genta] Yeah, I bet you're right.
-[Machu] The scenery would change too.

505
00:22:19,547 --> 00:22:22,007
[in English] We're gonna be coming up here
to a bridge, guys.

506
00:22:22,091 --> 00:22:23,634
-[Machu] Oh, really?
-You'll to be able to see it

507
00:22:23,717 --> 00:22:26,679
through the trees here.
The bridge is 130 years old…

508
00:22:26,762 --> 00:22:27,763
-Wow.
-…and it's gonna, uh,

509
00:22:27,847 --> 00:22:30,140
gonna take us
to the other side of the river.

510
00:22:30,224 --> 00:22:32,059
And it's over 100 feet long.

511
00:22:32,142 --> 00:22:34,812
And there's a curved section to it
on the north end.

512
00:22:34,895 --> 00:22:38,732
So, there's wood and steel sections
of this bridge that we're gonna cross.

513
00:22:38,816 --> 00:22:39,984
Right.

514
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:42,486
Bridge.

515
00:22:43,654 --> 00:22:44,655
Bridge.

516
00:22:45,447 --> 00:22:46,699
[Machu] Whoa.

517
00:22:47,283 --> 00:22:48,367
[Genta, in Japanese] Incredible.

518
00:22:48,450 --> 00:22:49,869
[whoops]

519
00:22:49,952 --> 00:22:51,662
[Machu] Whoa!

520
00:22:53,122 --> 00:22:54,290
Fantastic.

521
00:22:54,999 --> 00:22:56,000
[Genta] It feels incredible.

522
00:22:56,083 --> 00:22:57,084
[Machu] How nice.

523
00:22:58,043 --> 00:22:59,461
[Shime] The water is crystal clear.

524
00:22:59,545 --> 00:23:01,672
[Machu] Everything is breathtakingly
beautiful and refreshing.

525
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:03,173
-[Genta] Yeah.
-[Shime] Mm-hmm.

526
00:23:06,302 --> 00:23:08,304
[♪ serene music playing]

527
00:23:16,937 --> 00:23:18,939
[♪ music continues]

528
00:23:40,961 --> 00:23:42,963
[♪ music continues]

529
00:23:54,141 --> 00:23:55,142
[♪ music stops]

530
00:23:55,225 --> 00:23:57,227
[train chugging]

531
00:24:02,483 --> 00:24:03,984
[Genta, in Japanese] Shall we go
take a look at their drink selection?

532
00:24:04,068 --> 00:24:05,778
-Let's go hit up the shop. Yeah?
-[Machu] Let's go.

533
00:24:05,861 --> 00:24:07,863
-[Genta] Wanna go check it out?
-Wanna go check it out?

534
00:24:08,447 --> 00:24:09,907
-I wonder what they serve.
-Yeah.

535
00:24:15,663 --> 00:24:16,664
Thanks.

536
00:24:26,423 --> 00:24:28,133
-It's a shaky ride.
-[Genta] We're rocking.

537
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:37,726
[Genta, in English] Thank you.

538
00:24:40,521 --> 00:24:41,689
-[in Japanese] Awesome.
-Right?

539
00:24:41,772 --> 00:24:43,941
-[Machu] What a nice scent.
-[Genta] Yeah, the smell is heavenly.

540
00:24:44,525 --> 00:24:48,696
I've seen train stands
like this in movies.

541
00:24:48,779 --> 00:24:50,072
-[Genta] It's so cool.
-[Machu] Right?

542
00:24:51,907 --> 00:24:53,951
-They carry all sorts of drinks.
-Yeah, I've seen this in movies.

543
00:24:55,577 --> 00:24:57,204
I wonder if they serve coffee here.

544
00:24:57,287 --> 00:24:59,248
-[Genta] Oh, coffee sounds good.
-Good idea.

545
00:25:00,082 --> 00:25:03,377
For me, Coke maybe.

546
00:25:06,130 --> 00:25:08,007
-I love this vibe.
-Right?

547
00:25:08,757 --> 00:25:10,718
-[server, in English] Hi, my friends.
-Hi.

548
00:25:10,801 --> 00:25:11,802
-[server] How are you guys?
-Great.

549
00:25:11,885 --> 00:25:12,886
Really good.

550
00:25:13,429 --> 00:25:15,597
So, could I get Coke please?

551
00:25:15,681 --> 00:25:16,890
[server] A Coke?

552
00:25:16,974 --> 00:25:18,767
The blue bar down at the bottom.

553
00:25:21,145 --> 00:25:22,688
Uh, could I get coffee?

554
00:25:22,771 --> 00:25:24,273
-[server] Coffee?
-Yes, please. Thank you.

555
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:26,066
-[server] Do you like cream or sugar?
-No, black.

556
00:25:26,150 --> 00:25:28,068
-[server] Just black? You got it.
-Yes, thanks so much.

557
00:25:28,152 --> 00:25:29,737
[server]
I'll fill it all the way to the top.

558
00:25:29,820 --> 00:25:31,989
-Yeah.
-[train whistle blows]

559
00:25:33,449 --> 00:25:34,825
Can I get a water?

560
00:25:34,908 --> 00:25:35,909
-[server] A water?
-Yeah.

561
00:25:35,993 --> 00:25:38,120
It'll be in that refrigerator
right there for you at the bottom.

562
00:25:38,203 --> 00:25:39,204
Okay.

563
00:25:41,040 --> 00:25:42,041
Thank you so much.

564
00:25:42,124 --> 00:25:43,292
-[server] Absolutely.
-Thank you.

565
00:25:45,127 --> 00:25:46,253
[in Japanese] They serve it here.

566
00:25:48,213 --> 00:25:50,132
[train chugging]

567
00:25:50,215 --> 00:25:51,800
[train whistle blows]

568
00:25:55,971 --> 00:25:57,973
[♪ upbeat music playing]

569
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:01,810
[in English] Yeah. Hot dog!

570
00:26:01,894 --> 00:26:03,479
-Yeah.
-[in Japanese] Nice!

571
00:26:03,562 --> 00:26:04,813
[in English] Thank you.

572
00:26:04,897 --> 00:26:06,523
-Hot dog.
-[in Japanese] Thanks.

573
00:26:06,607 --> 00:26:07,608
This is the best.

574
00:26:07,691 --> 00:26:09,109
[in English] And then…
[in Japanese] Here you go.

575
00:26:09,193 --> 00:26:10,235
[in English] Oh, thank you.

576
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:13,197
-[in Japanese] Here.
-[in English] Thank you.

577
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,865
[Genta, in Japanese] This is the best.

578
00:26:16,366 --> 00:26:17,367
[Shime] Heck yeah!

579
00:26:19,661 --> 00:26:21,663
[Machu, in English] Oh, yeah!

580
00:26:21,747 --> 00:26:23,040
Oh, yeah.

581
00:26:24,708 --> 00:26:27,086
[Shime, in Japanese] Bon appétit!

582
00:26:27,169 --> 00:26:29,338
-[Machu, in English] Oh, yeah.
-[Genta] Oh, yes.

583
00:26:31,507 --> 00:26:33,217
[in Japanese] Don't eat without me, bro!

584
00:26:33,300 --> 00:26:36,553
I'll wait for you, bro.
I'll wait as long as you want me to, bro!

585
00:26:36,637 --> 00:26:38,305
-Wait, wait!
-Wait for me!

586
00:26:38,388 --> 00:26:40,099
-Take it easy, my man.
-[in English] Oh, yeah!

587
00:26:40,182 --> 00:26:43,685
[in Japanese] Time to dig in!

588
00:26:43,769 --> 00:26:45,395
-Time to dig in!
-Digging in.

589
00:26:48,357 --> 00:26:49,358
Yum!

590
00:26:49,441 --> 00:26:50,609
Scrumptious.

591
00:26:50,692 --> 00:26:52,277
The sausage's a killer.

592
00:26:52,361 --> 00:26:53,362
Delish.

593
00:26:56,615 --> 00:26:58,575
It's fantastic!

594
00:26:59,910 --> 00:27:01,995
So yummy!

595
00:27:02,079 --> 00:27:04,081
Scrumptious!

596
00:27:05,124 --> 00:27:06,792
Best hot dogs ever!

597
00:27:07,292 --> 00:27:08,460
[Genta, Machu laugh]

598
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:11,547
-Your voice squeaked.
-[Machu laughs]

599
00:27:13,340 --> 00:27:14,800
-This is crazy.
-Crazy!

600
00:27:17,886 --> 00:27:19,012
[Machu] It's the best.

601
00:27:20,514 --> 00:27:21,807
[Shime] This really is the best.

602
00:27:26,728 --> 00:27:27,813
-Mmm.
-[Genta] Mmm.

603
00:27:27,896 --> 00:27:29,064
Time to take a bite.

604
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:33,819
[Genta] It's amazing.

605
00:27:33,902 --> 00:27:34,987
[Machu] This is the best.

606
00:27:35,070 --> 00:27:36,196
Yum.

607
00:27:42,536 --> 00:27:44,204
[Genta] It's the best. What a nice breeze.

608
00:27:46,290 --> 00:27:48,709
[Machu shouting] It's the best.
What a nice breeze!

609
00:27:49,209 --> 00:27:50,210
[Shime whoops]

610
00:27:54,756 --> 00:27:56,174
[Machu] Are you getting hot?

611
00:27:56,800 --> 00:27:59,720
-[Genta] It's the best.
-[Machu] Oh, this is pure bliss.

612
00:28:01,096 --> 00:28:02,180
[Genta] I'm loving it.

613
00:28:04,057 --> 00:28:05,100
The bestest ever.

614
00:28:06,435 --> 00:28:07,644
Let's shout toward the valley, okay?

615
00:28:07,728 --> 00:28:08,854
[Genta, Machu] Ready, go.

616
00:28:08,937 --> 00:28:12,524
[all shouting]
Thanks for the scrumptious meal!

617
00:28:13,150 --> 00:28:14,151
[♪ music ends]

618
00:28:24,161 --> 00:28:25,746
[train whistle blowing]

619
00:28:33,253 --> 00:28:34,254
[Genta] We stopped.

620
00:28:35,047 --> 00:28:36,048
[static on radio]

621
00:28:38,008 --> 00:28:39,051
We stopped.

622
00:28:41,136 --> 00:28:42,721
[chattering on radio]

623
00:28:46,516 --> 00:28:47,601
Have we arrived?

624
00:28:49,770 --> 00:28:50,771
Is this it?

625
00:28:51,313 --> 00:28:52,397
[Shime] Maybe.

626
00:28:56,401 --> 00:28:57,903
[Genta] Even our stop screams America.

627
00:28:57,986 --> 00:28:59,154
[Machu laughs]

628
00:29:00,739 --> 00:29:01,740
It's not flat.

629
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:05,035
-[Genta] Wow…
-[Machu] Wow.

630
00:29:05,118 --> 00:29:07,537
[passenger speaking indistinctly
in English]

631
00:29:10,749 --> 00:29:11,750
[Machu, in Japanese] Whoa!

632
00:29:11,833 --> 00:29:13,669
-[Genta] Wow.
-[Shime] Amazing.

633
00:29:17,005 --> 00:29:18,882
Wow!

634
00:29:21,551 --> 00:29:23,261
-[Genta] This is incredible.
-Amazing.

635
00:29:24,638 --> 00:29:25,722
[chattering on radio]

636
00:29:27,766 --> 00:29:29,142
That's how the switch stand works.

637
00:29:30,102 --> 00:29:31,478
-Yeah. Cool, huh?
-Cool.

638
00:29:34,606 --> 00:29:35,732
It's wicked cool.

639
00:29:37,943 --> 00:29:38,944
[Machu] Huh.

640
00:29:40,821 --> 00:29:42,280
Amazing.

641
00:29:45,742 --> 00:29:46,952
That's impressive.

642
00:29:50,414 --> 00:29:53,083
Yes, now we're facing the front.

643
00:29:53,166 --> 00:29:55,210
-Mm-hmm.
-[Machu] You're right.

644
00:29:55,752 --> 00:29:58,255
-[chattering on radio]
-[Machu] Yes!

645
00:30:01,591 --> 00:30:02,884
[Shime] I see a station.

646
00:30:02,968 --> 00:30:04,302
-[Machu chuckles]
-[Genta] You sure?

647
00:30:04,386 --> 00:30:05,887
-Oh, a squirrel!
-[Machu] Where?

648
00:30:05,971 --> 00:30:06,805
[Shime] Where is it?

649
00:30:06,888 --> 00:30:08,807
[Genta] See the squirrel?
It's by the tracks. Right there.

650
00:30:18,817 --> 00:30:19,985
Did we pass a station?

651
00:30:20,068 --> 00:30:22,571
I was wrong.
Turns out it's a lodge, not a station.

652
00:30:24,448 --> 00:30:26,074
[Machu] What a nice breeze.

653
00:30:37,335 --> 00:30:40,047
[conductor, on radio, in English]
Train 265 to the dispatcher. Over.

654
00:30:46,595 --> 00:30:48,597
-[brakes squeak]
-[engine hissing]

655
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:52,684
We'll leave out of here at 12:45.

656
00:30:52,768 --> 00:30:54,019
[Genta] 12:45.

657
00:30:54,102 --> 00:30:57,856
We're gonna want all the passengers
back on the train by 12:35 at the latest.

658
00:30:57,939 --> 00:30:59,024
[Genta] All right.

659
00:30:59,107 --> 00:31:01,401
And I'll, uh, be letting you guys know
about some sights

660
00:31:01,485 --> 00:31:02,611
and things like that.

661
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:05,072
And we can show you
a couple really great views from up here.

662
00:31:05,155 --> 00:31:06,281
Sound good?

663
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:07,949
-[all] Okay. Yeah. Okay.
-All right.

664
00:31:09,201 --> 00:31:10,869
[♪ upbeat music playing]

665
00:31:19,628 --> 00:31:20,754
Oh, yeah.

666
00:31:20,837 --> 00:31:25,425
-[in Japanese] Whoa, how nice. I love it.
-[in English] Oh, yeah.

667
00:31:25,509 --> 00:31:26,760
[whoops]

668
00:31:27,344 --> 00:31:28,970
[♪ music continues]

669
00:31:34,601 --> 00:31:35,852
[Machu, in Japanese] How refreshing!

670
00:31:51,535 --> 00:31:52,536
[in English] Yeah.

671
00:31:52,619 --> 00:31:54,579
-[Shime, in Japanese] Is it cold?
-The water feels amazing.

672
00:31:54,663 --> 00:31:56,373
-Wanna come in?
-Like, actually?

673
00:31:56,957 --> 00:31:58,166
Gotta take off my shoes then.

674
00:31:58,250 --> 00:31:59,417
It's cold!

675
00:32:02,337 --> 00:32:05,048
-[laughs] It feels amazing.
-[Shime] That's cold!

676
00:32:05,132 --> 00:32:06,466
[Genta] Oh, the camera, the camera…

677
00:32:13,223 --> 00:32:14,474
[Machu, in English] Yeah.

678
00:32:17,269 --> 00:32:18,270
[in Japanese] Whoa.

679
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:20,564
[in English] Oh, yeah.

680
00:32:23,024 --> 00:32:24,943
[in Japanese] Here, Shime.
Wash your face with this.

681
00:32:29,322 --> 00:32:30,323
[♪ music stops]

682
00:32:35,954 --> 00:32:38,665
-Don't you want to blow the whistle?
-That sounds nice.

683
00:32:38,748 --> 00:32:40,041
Oh, sign me on. Heck yes!

684
00:32:51,887 --> 00:32:53,847
The train ride was so thrilling.

685
00:32:53,930 --> 00:32:55,307
The breeze was amazing.

686
00:32:55,390 --> 00:32:56,725
The scenery was to die for.

687
00:32:56,808 --> 00:32:58,476
-The breeze felt nice on my skin.
-[Genta] Mm-hmm.

688
00:32:58,560 --> 00:32:59,769
It was simply the best.

689
00:32:59,853 --> 00:33:02,981
I had three years' worth of fun
out in the wild.

690
00:33:04,107 --> 00:33:06,318
-[Shime] Three years?
-Three years' worth?

691
00:33:06,401 --> 00:33:08,236
Only three years? No more than that?

692
00:33:10,238 --> 00:33:12,866
-Make that five. [laughs]
-[Genta laughs]

693
00:33:14,284 --> 00:33:15,994
Yahoo. Try saying it.

694
00:33:16,077 --> 00:33:17,412
Yahoo.

695
00:33:17,495 --> 00:33:19,206
-Yahoo.
-Your turn.

696
00:33:19,289 --> 00:33:20,457
Yeah?

697
00:33:20,540 --> 00:33:21,541
This was a load of fun.

698
00:33:21,625 --> 00:33:23,668
-Right?
-Yeah, it was so refreshing.

699
00:33:23,752 --> 00:33:25,587
[Machu] We took in a breathtaking view
from the bridge too.

700
00:33:25,670 --> 00:33:26,671
The bridge was my favorite.

701
00:33:26,755 --> 00:33:29,591
And those tall rock walls.
It was a sight to behold.

702
00:33:29,674 --> 00:33:32,510
The rear compartments looked really slick
rounding that huge curve.

703
00:33:32,594 --> 00:33:33,678
-You mean the train?
-Yeah.

704
00:33:33,762 --> 00:33:35,513
-I feel you.
-It was amazing.

705
00:33:35,597 --> 00:33:37,182
-There's nothing like it.
-It was great.

706
00:33:37,807 --> 00:33:41,019
This was good. I'm glad
we had this experience with the train.

707
00:33:41,102 --> 00:33:42,312
[♪ gentle music playing]

708
00:33:42,395 --> 00:33:43,647
Don't you want to blow the whistle?

709
00:33:43,730 --> 00:33:45,690
-Make it go, "choo-choo."
-I wanted to make the train go choo-choo.

710
00:33:45,774 --> 00:33:47,275
-We can try asking?
-Let's at least ask.

711
00:33:47,359 --> 00:33:48,777
-There's no harm in asking.
-Yep.

712
00:33:48,860 --> 00:33:50,987
-We'll say we didn't get a chance earlier.
-Yeah.

713
00:33:53,573 --> 00:33:55,659
-[Machu] Wonder if they'll let us?
-[Genta] There's a chance.

714
00:33:57,702 --> 00:34:00,872
-[passenger, in English] Hello.
-[all] Hello.

715
00:34:06,336 --> 00:34:08,004
[in Japanese]
The front car is way up ahead.

716
00:34:08,088 --> 00:34:09,256
[Shime laughs]

717
00:34:09,339 --> 00:34:10,465
True that.

718
00:34:10,548 --> 00:34:12,509
This rest area is incredibly nice, huh?

719
00:34:12,592 --> 00:34:14,970
-It's chill.
-Isn't it chill? What?

720
00:34:15,053 --> 00:34:16,096
Let's all sprint…

721
00:34:16,179 --> 00:34:19,015
-[Machu] We'll race to the front…
-[Shime] Yeah, wanna race?

722
00:34:19,099 --> 00:34:21,726
-…then say… [in English] Let's go!
-[in Japanese] Let's do it.

723
00:34:21,810 --> 00:34:22,894
-[Genta] I'm down.
-Okay.

724
00:34:22,978 --> 00:34:25,230
-Yeah? You won't leave us hanging?
-[Genta] I bet he'll run with us.

725
00:34:25,313 --> 00:34:27,691
-I'll follow you the best I can.
-Then let's do it.

726
00:34:27,774 --> 00:34:28,775
-Promise, okay?
-Okay.

727
00:34:28,858 --> 00:34:29,859
-We're gonna race.
-Bring it on.

728
00:34:29,943 --> 00:34:31,528
Ready, go. Zoom!

729
00:34:33,905 --> 00:34:34,906
What's up?

730
00:34:35,532 --> 00:34:37,659
I'm feeling the groove.
I'm in the mood to dash.

731
00:34:37,742 --> 00:34:39,286
-You went all out?
-I did.

732
00:34:39,369 --> 00:34:40,870
Look at this crowd.

733
00:34:41,913 --> 00:34:43,373
They must be here
to look at the steam locomotive.

734
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:44,958
-Oh, you think?
-Yep.

735
00:34:45,041 --> 00:34:46,042
[♪ music ends]

736
00:34:48,586 --> 00:34:50,797
[conductor, in English] Four whistles
to get everybody back on the train.

737
00:34:50,880 --> 00:34:52,590
-Okay.
-Russell's gonna blow the first

738
00:34:52,674 --> 00:34:55,010
then each of you guys will take a turn
doing one whistle, okay?

739
00:34:55,093 --> 00:34:57,178
-All right.
-Right. Watch your step going up there.

740
00:34:57,262 --> 00:34:58,555
Okay, guys?

741
00:34:58,638 --> 00:34:59,848
[Genta] Right.

742
00:34:59,931 --> 00:35:01,558
[conductor] Watch your step
going up there. All right, guys?

743
00:35:01,641 --> 00:35:03,560
-Thank you so much. All right.
-Yeah, thank you.

744
00:35:03,643 --> 00:35:04,894
[in Japanese] Whoo-hoo!

745
00:35:05,395 --> 00:35:06,605
[in English] Yeah!

746
00:35:07,105 --> 00:35:08,857
[Genta, in Japanese]
I'm gonna blow the whistle!

747
00:35:10,567 --> 00:35:11,860
-I'm stoked.
-We're here.

748
00:35:11,943 --> 00:35:15,113
[Russell, in English] Okay. So,
the more you pull it, the louder it gets.

749
00:35:15,196 --> 00:35:17,324
-Okay.
-So, I'll only pull a little bit

750
00:35:17,407 --> 00:35:19,951
-because there's so many people around.
-[Machu] Okay, got it.

751
00:35:20,619 --> 00:35:22,954
[train whistle blowing]

752
00:35:27,375 --> 00:35:29,461
You're gonna hold it for like, three…
two or three seconds.

753
00:35:29,544 --> 00:35:32,213
-Like-Like that? Okay.
-Right. Yep. Yep, just like that.

754
00:35:32,297 --> 00:35:34,591
-[Shime, in Japanese] Whoa.
-Ready? Go.

755
00:35:36,217 --> 00:35:37,886
[train whistle blowing]

756
00:35:42,182 --> 00:35:44,017
-Whoa.
-[Shime] Nice!

757
00:35:44,100 --> 00:35:45,143
-[Genta] Amazing!
-[Machu] Just wow.

758
00:35:45,226 --> 00:35:46,686
[Shime] What an experience.

759
00:35:46,770 --> 00:35:47,771
We did it!

760
00:35:49,856 --> 00:35:51,441
-Ready?
-[Russell, in English] Yeah.

761
00:35:51,524 --> 00:35:53,318
[train whistle blowing]

762
00:35:56,780 --> 00:35:57,906
[Russell] Yeah.

763
00:35:59,616 --> 00:36:01,159
[in Japanese] Welp, I'm up.

764
00:36:03,536 --> 00:36:05,538
[train whistle blowing]

765
00:36:10,543 --> 00:36:12,629
-[Genta, Machu, Shime whoop]
-[Russell, in English] Yeah.

766
00:36:12,712 --> 00:36:14,923
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you so much.

767
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:16,841
-[Shime] Thank you.
-[Genta] Yeah. Thank you.

768
00:36:16,925 --> 00:36:19,177
-[Shime] It was so great.
-[Genta, in Japanese] This is crazy.

769
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:20,762
[Machu] Whoa. [laughs]

770
00:36:20,845 --> 00:36:22,055
[Shime, in English] Good experience.

771
00:36:22,138 --> 00:36:23,515
[Genta, in Japanese]
Everyone's gathered around.

772
00:36:23,598 --> 00:36:25,600
-[Machu, in English] Thank you so much.
-[Genta] Appreciate it.

773
00:36:26,101 --> 00:36:27,102
[Shime] Wow.

774
00:36:28,603 --> 00:36:29,854
[Genta, in Japanese] Here they come.

775
00:36:31,690 --> 00:36:33,066
It made me a tad emotional.

776
00:36:33,775 --> 00:36:35,026
[Machu] Heck yes.

777
00:36:35,110 --> 00:36:36,361
That was exhilarating.

778
00:36:36,444 --> 00:36:38,113
-[Genta] I'm satisfied.
-I'm so glad we asked.

779
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:41,324
-Who knew the train whistles were so loud?
-[Genta] Right?

780
00:36:41,408 --> 00:36:42,951
-It really rang out!
-[Machu] It was so loud.

781
00:36:43,034 --> 00:36:44,494
-It was crazy.
-[Genta, in English] Thank you so much.

782
00:36:44,577 --> 00:36:45,870
-Thank you so much.
-Thank you.

783
00:36:46,871 --> 00:36:47,872
Thank you.

784
00:36:47,956 --> 00:36:49,708
[in Japanese] Man, was that fun or what?

785
00:36:50,208 --> 00:36:51,334
They're all coming.

786
00:36:51,418 --> 00:36:52,711
-Everyone's gathering around.
-Yeah.

787
00:36:52,794 --> 00:36:54,963
-Because of our whistle.
-The train went, "choo-choo."

788
00:36:57,424 --> 00:36:58,508
Say cheese.

789
00:36:59,551 --> 00:37:00,635
[camera shutter clicks]

790
00:37:01,886 --> 00:37:02,971
[camera shutter clicks]

791
00:38:27,263 --> 00:38:29,224
Translated by Megumi Hunter
